\subsubsection{Dual de Hodge}

O dual de Hodge $\star: \Omega^p(\mathcal{M}) \to \Omega^{4-p}(\mathcal{M})$ é definido através da forma volume $\epsilon = \sqrt{-g} \, dx^0 \wedge dx^1 \wedge dx^2 \wedge dx^3$:

\begin{equation}

\begin{equation}
\star F_{\mu\nu} = \frac{1}{2}\frac{\epsilon_{\mu\nu\rho\sigma}}{\sqrt{-g}} F^{\rho\sigma}
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
F \wedge \star F = -\frac{1}{4}F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu} \sqrt{-g} \, d^4x
\label{eq:wedge_product}
\end{equation}

\end{definition}

Geometricamente, $g^{-1}$ "desfaz" a multiplicação por $\sqrt{-g}$ presente em \eqref{eq:wedge_product}, extraindo o invariante puro.

